{"qid":"Q1246","names":["Kosovo"],"title":"Kosovo","endonym":{"native":"Republika e Kosovës","lang":"sq"},"capsule":"Kosovo declared independence from Serbia on 17 February 2008, following a period of UN administration (UNMIK, established June 1999) that succeeded the NATO intervention ending Serbian military control. The declaration was supported by the United States and most EU member states; the International Court of Justice ruled in 2010 that the declaration did not violate international law. By the mid-2020s more than 110 UN member states had extended recognition, though Serbia, Russia, China, and several others have not, leaving Kosovo outside UN membership. Kosovo operates as a unitary parliamentary republic with Pristina as capital, is a member of the IMF and World Bank, and formally applied for EU membership in December 2022.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Kosovo's internationally recognized borders (those of the former Yugoslav autonomous province) are well-defined; de-facto administrative boundaries match them, though Serbia disputes their status.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Kosovo","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosovo"},{"label":"Britannica: Kosovo","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Kosovo"},{"label":"Wikipedia: 2008 Kosovo declaration of independence","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2008_Kosovo_declaration_of_independence"}],"britannica":"place/Kosovo","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Kosovo","rulers":[{"qid":"Q125794","name":"Bujar Bukoshi","start":1991,"end":2000,"image":"Bujar Bukoshi.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/